.SH Configuring autowt
\f[CR]autowt\f[R] is designed to work out of the box with sensible
defaults, but you can customize its behavior to perfectly match your
workflow.
This guide covers the different ways you can configure
\f[CR]autowt\f[R], from global settings to project\-specific rules and
one\-time command\-line overrides.
.PP
For a comprehensive example configuration file with comments explaining
all options, see the \c
.UR https://github.com/irskep/autowt/blob/main/example_config.toml
example_config.toml
.UE \c
\ in the repository.
.SS Configuration layers
\f[CR]autowt\f[R] uses a hierarchical configuration system.
Settings are loaded from multiple sources, and later sources override
earlier ones.
The order of precedence is:
.IP "1." 3
\f[B]Built\-in Defaults\f[R]: Sensible defaults for all settings.
.IP "2." 3
\f[B]Global \f[CB]config.toml\f[B]\f[R]: User\-wide settings that apply
to all your projects.
.IP "3." 3
\f[B]Project \f[CB].autowt.toml\f[B]\f[R]: Project\-specific settings,
defined in your repository\(cqs root.
.IP "4." 3
\f[B]Environment Variables\f[R]: System\-wide overrides, prefixed with
\f[CR]AUTOWT_\f[R].
.IP "5." 3
\f[B]Command\-Line Flags\f[R]: The highest priority, for on\-the\-fly
adjustments.
.SS Configuration files
.SS Global configuration
Your global settings are stored in a \f[CR]config.toml\f[R] file in a
platform\-appropriate directory:
.IP \(bu 2
\f[B]macOS\f[R]:
\f[CR]\(ti/Library/Application Support/autowt/config.toml\f[R]
.IP \(bu 2
\f[B]Linux\f[R]: \f[CR]\(ti/.config/autowt/config.toml\f[R] (or
\f[CR]$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/autowt/config.toml\f[R])
.IP \(bu 2
\f[B]Windows\f[R]: \f[CR]\(ti/.autowt/config.toml\f[R]
.PP
The easiest way to manage common settings is with the
\f[CR]autowt config\f[R] command, which launches an interactive TUI
(Text\-based User Interface) for the most frequently used options.
For the complete set of configuration options, you can edit the config
file directly.
.SS Project\-specific configuration
For settings that should apply only to a specific project, create a
\f[CR].autowt.toml\f[R] file in the root of your repository.
This is the ideal place to define project\-wide init scripts or worktree
settings.
.SS All configuration options
This section provides a comprehensive reference for all available
configuration options, organized by section.
Each option includes its TOML key, the corresponding environment
variable, and any command\-line flags.
