.SS \f[CR][scripts]\f[R] \- Lifecycle hooks and scripts
See Lifecycle Hooks.
.SS \f[CR][scripts.custom]\f[R]
Define named, reusable scripts for specialized workflows.
Custom scripts can be simple command strings or full workflow profiles
with their own lifecycle hooks and dynamic branch naming.
.SS Simple format
The simplest form is a command string that runs as
\f[CR]session_init\f[R].
For simple format scripts, the first CLI argument is used as the branch
name:
.IP
.EX
\f[B][scripts.custom]\f[R]
\f[I]# Simple: just a session_init command\f[R]
\f[I]# First argument ($1) becomes the branch name\f[R]
bugfix = \(aqclaude \(dqFix the bug described in GitHub issue $1\(dq\(aq
.EE
.PP
Usage: \f[CR]awt bugfix 123\f[R] creates a branch named \f[CR]123\f[R]
with the session_init command.
.SS Enhanced format
For more control, use a nested table to define a complete workflow
profile:
.IP
.EX
\f[B][scripts.custom.ghllm]\f[R]
\f[I]# Help text for \-\-help output\f[R]
description = \(dqCreate worktree from GitHub issue\(dq

\f[I]# Dynamic branch name from command output\f[R]
branch_name = \(dqgh issue view $1 \-\-json title \-\-template \(aq{{.title}}\(aq\(dq

\f[I]# Hook inheritance (default: true)\f[R]
inherit_hooks = true

\f[I]# Any lifecycle hook can be overridden\f[R]
pre_create = \(dqecho \(aqStarting ghllm workflow\(aq\(dq
session_init = \(aqclaude \(dqWork on GitHub issue $1\(dq\(aq
.EE
