.SS Argument interpolation
All string fields support \f[CR]$1\f[R], \f[CR]$2\f[R], \f[CR]$3\f[R],
etc.
placeholders that are replaced with arguments passed to the custom
script:
.IP
.EX
\f[I]# Invoke custom script directly (recommended)\f[R]
awt ghllm 123

\f[I]# Or using the legacy flag\f[R]
awt \-\-custom\-script=\(dqghllm 123\(dq

\f[I]# $1 is replaced with \(dq123\(dq in all fields\f[R]
.EE
.SS Dynamic branch naming
When \f[CR]branch_name\f[R] is set, the command is executed and its
stdout becomes the branch name.
The output is automatically normalized to be a valid git ref:
.IP \(bu 2
Converted to lowercase
.IP \(bu 2
Spaces and underscores become dashes
.IP \(bu 2
Invalid git ref characters are removed
.IP \(bu 2
Double dots, consecutive dashes/slashes are collapsed
.PP
Example transformations:
.PP
.TS
tab(@);
l l.
T{
Command output
T}@T{
Resulting branch name
T}
_
T{
\f[CR]Fix the login bug\f[R]
T}@T{
\f[CR]fix\-the\-login\-bug\f[R]
T}
T{
\f[CR]Feature: Add OAuth\f[R]
T}@T{
\f[CR]feature\-add\-oauth\f[R]
T}
T{
\f[CR][BUG] Crash on startup\f[R]
T}@T{
\f[CR]bug\-crash\-on\-startup\f[R]
T}
T{
\f[CR]feature/Add user auth\f[R]
T}@T{
\f[CR]feature/add\-user\-auth\f[R]
T}
.TE
.SS Hook inheritance
When \f[CR]inherit_hooks = true\f[R] (the default), hooks run in this
order:
.IP "1." 3
Global config hook (if defined)
.IP "2." 3
Project config hook (if defined)
.IP "3." 3
Custom script hook (if defined)
.PP
When \f[CR]inherit_hooks = false\f[R], only the custom script\(cqs hooks
run; global and project hooks are skipped.
.SS Example workflows
\f[B]GitHub issue workflow\f[R] \- Creates a branch named after the
issue title:
.IP
.EX
\f[B][scripts.custom.ghissue]\f[R]
branch_name = \(dqgh issue view $1 \-\-json title \-\-template \(aq{{.title}}\(aq\(dq
session_init = \(aqclaude \(dqWork on GitHub issue $1: $(gh issue view $1 \-\-json title \-\-template \(aq\f[B]\(rs\f[R]\(aq\(aq\f[B]{{\f[R].title\f[B]}}\f[R]\(aq\(rs\(aq\(aq)\(dq\(aq
.EE
.PP
\f[B]Release workflow\f[R] \- Custom pre_create and session_init:
.IP
.EX
\f[B][scripts.custom.release]\f[R]
inherit_hooks = false  \f[I]# Skip normal hooks\f[R]
pre_create = \(dqgit fetch \-\-tags\(dq
session_init = \(aqclaude \(dq/release\(dq\(aq
.EE
.PP
Custom scripts are invoked directly as subcommands:
.IP
.EX
\f[I]# Enhanced format (branch_name field) \- issue number is an argument\f[R]
awt ghissue 123

\f[I]# Simple format \- first argument is used as the branch name\f[R]
awt release release\-v2.0
.EE
.PP
\f[B]Resolution priority\f[R]: When \f[CR]autowt\f[R] receives an
unknown command, it checks in this order:
.IP "1." 3
Built\-in commands (\f[CR]ls\f[R], \f[CR]cleanup\f[R],
\f[CR]config\f[R], \f[CR]switch\f[R], and their aliases)
.IP "2." 3
Custom scripts (matches against \f[CR][scripts.custom]\f[R] names)
.IP "3." 3
Branch names (treats the command as a branch to switch to)
.PP
If you have a custom script named \f[CR]main\f[R] and want to switch to
a branch named \f[CR]main\f[R], use \f[CR]awt switch main\f[R] to force
branch interpretation.
